  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "49c69893-3fb4-4a8e-99a2-8b700326cda5",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        512,
        -416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 540,
        "height": 1300,
        "content": "# Migrate SmartSuite attachments into Monday.com\n\nMove every file attached to your SmartSuite records into the files column of the matching Monday.com item. Useful as a one-off migration when a team moves from SmartSuite to Monday, so documents and images travel with the records instead of being left behind.\n\n### How it works\n1. A manual trigger starts the run and one Set node holds every API key and ID.\n2. Records are pulled from a SmartSuite table, and a Code node flattens them so each attached file becomes its own item.\n3. Files are processed one at a time. For each file the matching Monday item is found by searching a text column for the SmartSuite record ID. Files with no match are skipped and the loop continues.\n4. A temporary download URL is requested from SmartSuite, the file is downloaded, then uploaded straight into the Monday files column.\n5. A short delay after each upload keeps the run inside Monday's rate limits.\n\n### Setup\nOpen the Set config variables node and replace every placeholder:\n- SmartSuite API key: SmartSuite profile menu, API section.\n- SmartSuite workspace ID and table ID: both appear in the table's URL.\n- File field slugs: the SmartSuite field IDs of your file columns, comma separated.\n- Monday API key: Monday avatar menu, Developers, My access tokens.\n- Monday board ID: the number in the board URL.\n- Monday text column ID: the column holding the SmartSuite record ID, used for matching.\n- Monday files column ID: the column that will receive the files.\n\n### Customization\nRaise batch_limit or move current_offset to migrate a large table page by page."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fcb6ec85-7352-4ab2-b6b3-cb84a314ee38",
